==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|récidivisme}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|recidīvus||returning, recurring}} (compare {{term|recidivous}}) {{suffix||ism|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# repeated or habitual relapse, as into  [[crime]].
#: ''The increase in criminal activity was attributed to [[recidivism]].''
# {{label|en|psychology|psychiatry}} [[chronic|Chronic]] [[repetition]] of [[criminal]] or other [[antisocial]] behavior.
# {{label|en|by extension}} Returning to a negative [[behavior]] after having stopped it for a period of time.
#: ''alcohol(ic) '''recidivism'''''

